  "hypothesis": "Increasing NEON SIMD batch size from 4 to 8 points per iteration using vld1q_f32_x2 reduces loop overhead and improves vector utilization. Adding restrict qualifiers on xs/ys pointers in Group struct eliminates aliasing concerns, enabling better compiler optimization of memory accesses. Hoisting invariant point coordinates outside the inner batch loop further reduces redundant broadcast instructions. These changes maintain correctness while improving SIMD throughput for distance computation.",
